{"id": "EUVD-2026-108134", "enisaUuid": "d4e189ab-856a-39c5-907c-20eba9fed5a7", "description": "Lotus through 0.10.2 contains an sql injection vulnerability that allows authenticated organization users to inject SQL by registering crafted subscription_filter_keys that bypass keyword-only validation. Attackers can create subscriptions using the malicious key, which is rendered as an unquoted group-by identifier, to inject SQL into usage aggregation queries against the shared multi-tenant database.", "datePublished": "2026-10-22T10:57:48", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-22T10:57:48", "baseScore": 8.7, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@leediay/BkUc3WL2Mx", "https://github.com/uselotus/lotus/blob/0.10.2/backend/metering_billing/serializers/model_serializers.py#L518-L534", "https://github.com/uselotus/lotus", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/lotus-through-0.10.2-sql-injection-via-subscription-filter-keys"], "aliases": ["GHSA-fcf4-2wr8-2h4q", "CVE-2026-115332"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.0, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "5a871169-7c06-3bab-8aa8-efb20cc98b43", "product": {"name": "lotus", "vendor": {"name": "filecoin-project"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22640.10.2"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "116064df-5376-33d2-b5af-9b631438801d", "vendor": {"name": "uselotus"}}], "isExploited": false}